{"id":"understand-geotech-esa-flex-launch","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"精选主稿：欧洲空间局一手发射通报。","match":{"urlIncludes":"FLEX_and_Sentinel-3C_launched","titleIncludes":"FLEX and Sentinel-3C"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.esa.int/Applications/Observing_the_Earth/FLEX_and_Sentinel-3C_launched","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"ESA Observing the Earth","title":"FLEX and Sentinel-3C launched","text":"FLEX and Sentinel-3C launched — ESA / Applications / Observing the Earth, 15/09/2026.\n\nFlight VV30 lifted off on 15 September at 03:21 (14 September at 22:21 local time).\n\nA launch adapter called Vespa allowed both satellites to be stacked inside the Vega-C fairing for launch. Positioned on top of Vespa, Sentinel-3C was injected into orbit first, followed by FLEX approximately one hour later.\n\nFollowing the satellites’ separate deployments, ESA’s European Space Operations Centre in Germany received the all-important first signal from each satellite, confirming that both had been safely released from the rocket and had established contact with ground control.\n\nMission controllers will now spend the coming days conducting the ‘launch and early orbit phase’, meticulously checking and verifying the health and performance of both satellites and confirming that all systems are functioning as expected.\n\nESA’s Director of Earth Observation Programmes, Simonetta Cheli, said, “Today’s launch is the culmination of years of scientific innovation, engineering excellence and international cooperation.\n\n“Developed within ESA’s FutureEO programme, FLEX is a research mission that will advance our understanding of plant health and the role of photosynthesis in the carbon and water cycles. Sentinel-3C is the third satellite in the Sentinel-3 series, systematically measuring Earth’s oceans, land, ice and atmosphere to support Europe’s Copernicus Services.\n\n“Preparing and launching two satellites together is no easy task. My thanks go to the many experts who have contributed throughout both satellites’ development, testing and preparation for launch, and who have worked tirelessly to ensure that both satellites have reached orbit safely.”\n\nFLEX to reveal the hidden activity of Earth’s vegetation\n\nFLEX, the latest Earth Explorer mission, is ESA’s first satellite designed specifically to measure photosynthetic activity from space. Its Fluorescence Imaging Spectrometer will detect the extremely faint fluorescence emitted by plants as they absorb sunlight during photosynthesis."},"reply":{"itemType":"technology_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["技术与软件","遥感影像","欧空局","哥白尼计划"],"editorialJudgment":"双星同乘一枚 Vega-C：FLEX 是首颗专门观测植被荧光以研究光合作用的卫星，Sentinel-3C 接续 Sentinel-3 对海洋、陆地、冰雪与大气的长期记录。这是“能观测到什么”的改变，不是在轨运行例行通报；发射时刻、堆叠方式、分离顺序与首次信号都可核验。","titleZh":"欧洲空间局（ESA）：FLEX 与哥白尼（Copernicus）Sentinel-3C 双星发射入轨","summaryZh":"9 月 15 日 03:21 UTC，欧洲空间局（ESA）的 FLEX 与哥白尼（Copernicus）Sentinel-3C 同乘一枚 Vega-C 火箭从库鲁发射，借助 Vespa 适配器堆叠：Sentinel-3C 先入轨，约 1 小时后 FLEX 分离，地面站随即收到双星首次信号。FLEX 观测植物荧光以研究光合作用，Sentinel-3C 继续海洋、陆地、冰雪与大气的长期记录。"}}
{"id":"understand-geotech-noaa-fim","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"精选主稿：NOAA 一手发布，覆盖范围变化。","match":{"urlIncludes":"noaa-flood-mapping-tool","titleIncludes":"flood mapping tool"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.noaa.gov/news-release/noaa-flood-mapping-tool-now-covers-nearly-100-of-us","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"NOAA News Releases","title":"NOAA’s flood mapping tool now covers nearly 100% of U.S.","text":"Experimental Flood Inundation Mapping provides valuable guidance for decision-makers and public\n\nNOAA's flood inundation map (left) depicting the forecast for flooding extent in New London, Wisconsin, and a photo of flooded streets in New London (right), dated April 17, 2026. (Image credit: NOAA NWS)\n\nNOAA’s National Weather Service announced today that Flood Inundation Mapping (FIM), a revolutionary tool for predicting river flooding, is now available on an experimental basis to nearly 100% of the U.S. population. This is a massive expansion from FIM’s prior coverage of 60% of the country.\n\nFIM produces estimates of land area covered in water based on model forecast river flows and current conditions that predict where flooding impacts may occur in the following days. It’s a tool for forecasters, emergency managers and the public that alerts users to the latest river and stream flooding conditions.\n\n“Inundation maps are a critical tool for assessing the impacts of flooding,” said NOAA Administrator Neil Jacobs, Ph.D. “NOAA prioritized expanding FIM to ensure that nearly every American can access detailed information beyond the expected river crest height. These maps further support NOAA's mission to protect lives, safeguard property, and strengthen our national economy.”\n\nFIM puts river and stream flooding on the map at a neighborhood scale. It depicts flooding potential along 3.3 million river miles throughout the continental U.S., U.S. territories and Hawaii. For the most recent expansion, FIM’s new coverage areas include: the southeastern U.S. coast and Florida; Great Lakes region; New England; the Rocky Mountains; the Dakotas; and western Nebraska.\n\nFIM has already helped the NWS understand, assess and communicate maximum river flood potential to emergency management personnel, medical care facilities, and other critical decision makers. Success stories from local NWS offices include:\n\nNWS’s office in Nashville, TN used FIM to provide a Senior Assisted Living facility in Macon County information to safely evacuate residents in the spring of 2025, hours before"},"reply":{"itemType":"technology_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["技术与软件","GIS与空间数据","预警/响应","NOAA"],"editorialJudgment":"覆盖范围改变型发布：试验运行的洪水淹没制图（FIM）由 60% 扩展到近 100% 美国人口，沿 3.3 million 英里河流给出社区尺度淹没范围，预报员、应急管理者与公众今天就能调用。按可用性型正常评价，不套“厂商版本通告”上限。","titleZh":"美国国家海洋和大气管理局（NOAA）洪水淹没制图 FIM 覆盖近 100% 美国人口","summaryZh":"美国国家海洋和大气管理局（NOAA）国家气象局宣布，洪水淹没制图（Flood Inundation Mapping，FIM）以试验形式覆盖近 100% 的美国人口，此前仅为 60%。FIM 沿美国本土、属地与夏威夷的 3.3 million 英里河流，依预报流量与当前状况估算被水覆盖的地表范围，达到社区尺度，供预报员、应急管理者与公众使用。"},"dissent":[{"id":"understand-cl16","capability":"understand","theme":"climate","author":"地理编辑（气候与观测数据 beat）","at":"corpus-climate-brain.jsonl#L54","why":"同一份材料两份中文稿：本桌按 technology_release/principal 写（与本项目里它的 scores、structure 三条同口径），气候桌按 observation_release 写。采本桌。气候桌那份（整修时刚把摘要里的「应急管理部门」改成「应急响应人员」以避开实体别名 mem=应急管理部）整份留档在这里，一句不丢。","match":{"urlIncludes":"flood-mapping-tool-now-covers"},"reply":{"itemType":"observation_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["观测/数据发布","洪水与干旱","水资源","NOAA"],"editorialJudgment":"国家级洪水淹没制图把覆盖人口从 60% 扩到近 100%，是可核验的能力变化，但属工具覆盖通告，正文写明 experimental，摘要不加已全面业务化的推断。","titleZh":"NOAA洪水淹没制图扩至近100%美国人口","summaryZh":"NOAA 国家气象局宣布，河流洪水淹没制图（FIM）已以试验方式向近 100% 的美国人口开放，此前覆盖为 60%。FIM 依据模式预测的河流流量与当前状况估算被水覆盖的地表范围，服务预报员、应急响应人员与公众。"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.noaa.gov/news-release/noaa-flood-mapping-tool-now-covers-nearly-100-of-us","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"NOAA","title":"NOAA’s flood mapping tool now covers nearly 100% of U.S.","text":"Experimental Flood Inundation Mapping provides valuable guidance for decision-makers and public\n\nNOAA's flood inundation map (left) depicting the forecast for flooding extent in New London, Wisconsin, and a photo of flooded streets in New London (right), dated April 17, 2026. (Image credit: NOAA NWS)\n\nNOAA’s National Weather Service announced today that Flood Inundation Mapping (FIM), a revolutionary tool for predicting river flooding, is now available on an experimental basis to nearly 100% of the U.S. population. This is a massive expansion from FIM’s prior coverage of 60% of the country.\n\nFIM produces estimates of land area covered in water based on model forecast river flows and current conditions that predict where flooding impacts may occur in the following days. It’s a tool for forecasters, emergency managers and the public that alerts users to the latest river and stream flooding conditions.\n\n“Inundation maps are a critical tool for assessing the impacts of flooding,” said NOAA Administrator Neil Jacobs, Ph.D. “NOAA prioritized expanding FIM to ensure that nearly every American can access detailed information beyond the expected river crest height. These maps further support NOAA's mission to protect lives, safeguard property, and strengthen our national economy.”\n\nFIM puts river and stream flooding on the map at a neighborhood scale. It depicts flooding potential along 3.3 million river miles throughout the continental U.S., U.S. territories and Hawaii. For the most recent expansion, FIM’s new coverage areas include: the southeastern U.S. coast and Florida; Great Lakes region; New England; the Rocky Mountains; the Dakotas; and western Nebraska.\n\nFIM has already helped the NWS understand, assess and communicate maximum river flood potential to emergency management personnel, medical care facilities, and other critical decision makers. Success stories from local NWS offices include:\n\nNWS’s office in Nashville, TN used FIM to provide a Senior Assisted Living facility in Macon County information to safely evacuate residents in the spring of 2025, hours before"}}]}
{"id":"understand-geotech-gsc-sas","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"精选主稿：GSC 一手服务里程碑。","match":{"urlIncludes":"galileo-achieves-first-ever","titleIncludes":"first-ever civil authenticated"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.gsc-europa.eu/news/galileo-achieves-first-ever-civil-authenticated-gnss-position-using-signal-authentication","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"European GNSS Service Centre (GSC)","title":"Galileo achieves first-ever civil authenticated GNSS position using Signal Authentication Service (SAS)","text":"European GNSS Service Centre (GSC) news, 17 September 2026.\n\nOn 16 September, Galileo achieved a major milestone in satellite navigation resilience by demonstrating the first-ever civil GNSS position authenticated through both navigation data and ranging information. The demonstration used the Galileo Signal Authentication Service (SAS) concept, with five Galileo satellites transmitting encrypted signal components over Europe. Receivers on the ground successfully processed these signals to compute an authenticated position fix, demonstrating a new level of protection for civil satellite navigation.\n\nOn 16 September, between 14:00 and 16:00 UTC, five Galileo satellites—E06, E21, E23, E34 and E36—encrypted one of their signal components, the E6-C signal at 1278.75 MHz, normally transmitted in the clear. Several Galileo SAS receivers deployed at different locations successfully processed these signals in combination with Galileo Open Service Navigation Message Authentication (OSNMA) . For the first time, a civil GNSS receiver was able to process authenticated navigation data and ranging measurements from at least four satellites simultaneously and compute an authenticated position fix.\n\nA significant part of the demonstration took place during Jammertest on the island of Andøya, Norway, where controlled GNSS jamming and spoofing tests are conducted using real over-the-air signals. This provided a unique opportunity to evaluate Galileo SAS under both nominal conditions and many types of spoofing.\n\nDuring the spoofing tests, conventional receivers were deceived and reported false positions, while the Galileo SAS receiver detected the attack and maintained a trusted position solution based on authenticated Galileo signals.\n\nHistorically, civil GNSS receivers have had limited means to verify that the signals they use genuinely originate from navigation satellites. Galileo addressed part of this vulnerability through OSNMA, declared operational in 2025, which authenticates the navigation data transmitted by Galileo satellites. SAS complements OSNMA by protecting the other fundamental source of information used to compute a GNSS position: the ranging measurements."},"reply":{"itemType":"technology_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["技术与软件","卫星导航"],"editorialJudgment":"导航系统能力节点：首次同时认证导航电文与测距量的民用定位，硬标识齐全（5 颗卫星编号、E6-C 1278.75 MHz、UTC 时段、挪威 Jammertest 的抗欺骗验证）。改变的是“定位结果能否被验证”；仍处演示阶段，act 保守给 4。","titleZh":"Galileo 完成首次经认证民用定位：SAS 与 OSNMA 联合验证","summaryZh":"9 月 16 日 14:00—16:00 UTC，Galileo 的 E06、E21、E23、E34、E36 五颗卫星加密了通常明文发射的 E6-C 信号（1278.75 MHz）。欧洲 GNSS 服务中心（European GNSS Service Centre）称，多地接收机把它与开放服务导航电文认证（OSNMA）联用，首次同时解算至少 4 颗卫星的认证电文与测距量，算出经认证位置。"}}
{"id":"understand-geotech-c3s-cds","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"精选主稿：哥白尼一手数据集发布。","match":{"urlIncludes":"new-datasets-expand","titleIncludes":"New datasets expand"},"guard":{"url":"https://climate.copernicus.eu/new-datasets-expand-climate-data-stores-window-earths-changing-climate","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"Copernicus Climate Change Service","title":"New datasets expand the Climate Data Store’s window on Earth’s changing climate","text":"Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S), implemented by ECMWF — press article, 17 June 2026.\n\nThe Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S) has expanded its Climate Data Store ( CDS ) with a new suite of datasets. Spanning the atmosphere, land, ocean, cryosphere and water cycle, these additions provide new opportunities to explore how the Earth system is changing and how those changes affect people, ecosystems and infrastructure. Of the new additions to the CDS, some datasets extend climate records further back in time, others deliver sharper regional detail, while others translate climate observations into practical information relevant to topics such as water resources, heat stress and energy systems, helping users better understand the real-world impacts of climate variability and change. Let's take a closer look.\n\nOn land, the Global land surface atmospheric variables from 1718 to present from comprehensive in-situ observations dataset offers one of the longest meteorological records available through the CDS. Drawing on observations from weather stations around the world, it provides harmonised and quality-controlled records of key atmospheric variables spanning more than three centuries. The dataset supports investigations into long-term climate variability and change, while also providing an important observational foundation for the development and validation of climate datasets and reanalyses.\n\nLand-based stations available in the latest version of the Global land surface atmospheric variables from 1718 to present from comprehensive in-situ observations, with sub-daily data. Source: C3S\n\nThe historical picture is further strengthened by the ORAS5 global ocean reanalysis monthly data from 1958 to present dataset , which reconstructs ocean conditions by assimilating observations with advanced ocean and sea-ice modelling. Covering more than six decades, ORAS5 provides a consistent record of ocean temperature, salinity, currents, sea level and sea-ice properties, supporting research into ocean variability, heat uptake, circulation patterns and the ocean's role in climate change.\n\nCompleting the picture, the Near surface meteorological variables from 1979 to p"},"reply":{"itemType":"observation_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["观测/数据发布","GIS与空间数据","气候异常","哥白尼计划"],"editorialJudgment":"新增免费公开数据集：CDS 一次扩充跨大气、陆地、海洋、冰冻圈与水循环的成套数据，把可分析的时间窗向前推（1718 年至今、ORAS5 1958 年至今、偏差订正再分析 1979 年至今），并提供更细的北极区域分辨率。属基准数据集层面的可观测能力变化，可下载可复用。","titleZh":"哥白尼气候变化服务扩充气候数据仓库（CDS）数据集","summaryZh":"哥白尼气候变化服务（Copernicus Climate Change Service，C3S）扩充气候数据仓库（Climate Data Store，CDS），新增数据集覆盖大气、陆地、海洋、冰冻圈与水循环。其中 1718 年至今的全球陆地地表大气变量把地面气象记录延长三个多世纪，ORAS5 海洋再分析月值数据（1958 年至今）与 1979 年至今的偏差订正再分析变量同时入库。"}}
{"id":"understand-geotech-c3s-august","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"精选主稿：哥白尼月度观测发布（含异常值）。","match":{"urlIncludes":"august-was-joint-warmest","titleIncludes":"joint warmest month"},"guard":{"url":"https://climate.copernicus.eu/august-was-joint-warmest-month-ever-recorded-globally-temperatures-once-again-exceeding-15degc","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"Copernicus Climate Change Service","title":"August was the joint warmest month ever recorded globally","text":"Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S) Climate Bulletin, implemented by ECMWF — published 16 September 2026.\n\nAugust was the joint warmest month ever recorded globally, with temperatures once again exceeding 1.5&#176;C above pre-industrial levels\n\nAugust 2026 was the joint hottest month on record worldwide, tied with July 2023, as reported in the latest Climate Bulletin by Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S) 1 . The month also saw the average sea surface temperature (SST) over the extra-polar ocean &#8211; between 60&#176;S and 60&#176;N &#8211; reach a record high. This new record can be explained by global heating from burning fossil fuels and rapidly increasing SSTs in the equatorial Pacific, which were associated with strong El Ni&#241;o conditions.\n\nGlobal-average surface air temperature (&#176;C) for 2023 (orange), 2024 (yellow), and 2026 (dark red). All other years between 1940 and 2025 are shown with grey lines. Data source: ERA5. Credit: C3S/ECMWF.\n\nGlobally, the average surface air temperature in August was 16.96&#176;C, making it the hottest month ever recorded (for all calendar months), tied with July 2023. Notably, this temperature was 1.65&#176;C higher than the estimated 1850-1900 pre-industrial baseline for the month, putting the world once again over 1.5&#176;C above pre-industrial levels. The last time this value was exceeded was less than a year ago, in November 2025. Additionally, it was the warmest August ever recorded, surpassing the previous joint August record, which was set in 2023 and 2024.\n\nThe month marked the end of the world's joint hottest June to August period on record, tied with 2024. August also saw the end of western Europe's warmest summer ever recorded, which exceeded the previous long-standing record set in 2003. Western Europe's summer was marked by a succession of intense heatwaves across the region &#8211; a sequence that began exceptionally early and continued throughout the season."},"reply":{"itemType":"observation_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["观测/数据发布","气候异常","哥白尼计划"],"editorialJudgment":"月度气候统计出现异常值与创纪录口径，因此不适用“例行数据更新 sig ≤ 3”：16.96 °C 与 2023 年 7 月并列全部月份最高，超出 1850—1900 基线 1.65 °C，60°S—60°N 海表温度创纪录，量值可由 ERA5 复核。数据发布与气候结论并存时按发布口径归类本领域。","titleZh":"哥白尼：2026 年 8 月为有记录以来并列最热月份","summaryZh":"哥白尼气候变化服务（C3S）最新气候公报（Climate Bulletin）以 ERA5 判定，2026 年 8 月全球平均地表气温 16.96 °C，与 2023 年 7 月并列为所有月份中最高，比 1850—1900 年工业化前基线高 1.65 °C；60°S—60°N 的海表温度创下纪录，西欧夏季超过 2003 年纪录。"},"dissent":[{"id":"understand-cl04","capability":"understand","theme":"climate","author":"地理编辑（气候与观测数据 beat）","at":"corpus-climate-brain.jsonl#L57","why":"同一份材料两份中文稿：采本桌（每个数都能在标准件正文里核到，并明确处理了「例行数据更新 sig≤3」这条硬上限为何不适用）。气候桌那份的摘要写了「非极地海表温度 21.07°C」——这个数在两份副本正文里都不存在（原文只说 reach a record high），不采信，整份留档待核。","match":{"urlIncludes":"august-was-joint-warmest-month-ever-recorded"},"reply":{"itemType":"observation_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["观测/数据发布","气候异常","海洋","哥白尼计划"],"editorialJudgment":"这是该次月度发布的通报口径，把气温、非极地海表温度与干旱并置，并给出超 1.5°C 的单月读数；单月超阈不等于《巴黎协定》长期目标突破，摘要不加这一层推断。","titleZh":"8月全球气温超工业化前1.65°C，并列最热月","summaryZh":"C3S 月度通报，2026 年 8 月全球平均地表气温 16.96°C，与 2023 年 7 月并列有记录最热，较 1850-1900 年工业化前基线高 1.65°C，是自 2025 年 11 月以来再次超过 1.5°C。同月非极地海洋（60°S—60°N）海表温度 21.07°C，与 2024 年 3 月并列有记录最高。"},"guard":{"url":"https://climate.copernicus.eu/august-was-joint-warmest-month-ever-recorded-globally-temperatures-once-again-exceeding-15degc","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"Copernicus Climate Change Service","title":"August was the joint warmest month ever recorded globally, with temperatures once again exceeding 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels","text":"Globally, the average surface air temperature in August was 16.96°C, making it the hottest month ever recorded (for all calendar months), tied with July 2023. Notably, this temperature was 1.65°C higher than the estimated 1850-1900 pre-industrial baseline for the month, putting the world once again over 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels. The month also saw the average sea surface temperature (SST) over the extra-polar ocean – between 60°S and 60°N – reach a record high."}}]}
{"id":"understand-geotech-nasa-greenland","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"精选主稿：NASA 新图与新方法。","match":{"urlIncludes":"uncovering-the-valleys","titleIncludes":"Valleys Hidden Below Greenland"},"guard":{"url":"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/uncovering-the-valleys-hidden-below-greenlands-ice/","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"NASA Earth Observatory","title":"Uncovering the Valleys Hidden Below Greenland’s Ice","text":"NASA Earth Observatory, Image of the Day, published 28 September 2026 — 4 min read.\n\nA new map of the terrain beneath the Greenland Ice Sheet links hundreds of valleys that previous maps missed or left fragmented.\n\nInstruments: ICESat-2 — ATLAS Model Topics: Glaciers & Ice Sheets Topography Visualization and Mapping A newly developed method for mapping the bedrock beneath Greenland’s ice sheet reveals the island’s hidden topography. Among the most striking finds are long, straight valleys in the west-central region, some mapped for the first time and others extending farther inland than previously known (inset 3). NASA Earth Observatory/Lauren Dauphin, based on data from Chartrand et al . Greenland is capped with a vast ice sheet that spans 1.7 million square kilometers (656,000 square miles) and measures more than 3 kilometers (1.9 miles) at its thickest point. Below all this ice lies a landscape human eyes have never seen directly. But a newly developed method for mapping this hidden bedrock has produced the most detailed and accurate view of it yet.\n\nThe new map reveals an expansive network of valleys carved into the surface beneath the Greenland Ice Sheet. Many of the features formed well before most of the ice above them existed, offering new context for the island’s geologic history—and potentially helping scientists refine projections of the ice sheet’s future. Scientists described the newly mapped valleys in a NASA-led paper published in Geophysical Research Letters .\n\nThe map, shown above, was derived from a method called Ice Flow Perturbation Analysis. As ice flows over a valley or ridge, the topography leaves a faint signature on the ice surface. Satellites map the ice surface in fine detail, and scientists can use these subtle bumps and dips to infer the shape of the landscape buried below. The work aims to improve future versions of BedMachine Greenland , a high-resolution dataset of the terrain beneath the ice sheet.\n\nUsing the technique, researchers manually mapped 1,943 subglacial valleys beneath the Greenland Ice Sheet, about a third of which are newly identified. About half of the valleys included in BedMachine Greenland, primarily near the ice"},"reply":{"itemType":"observation_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["观测/数据发布","遥感影像","冰川与冻土","NASA"],"editorialJudgment":"制图与数据产品型发布：新的冰盖基床测绘方法把数百条此前遗漏或零散的山谷连成网络，改变的是“能看到什么基底地形”，不是又一篇单点方法论文。ICESat-2 — ATLAS 与 Chartrand et al. 给出可核验来源与范围。","titleZh":"新方法绘出格陵兰冰盖之下基岩山谷网络","summaryZh":"美国国家航空航天局（NASA）地球观测站介绍一项新的冰盖基岩测绘方法，绘出迄今最详细、最准确的格陵兰冰盖基底地形图，把数百条此前被遗漏或零散的山谷连接起来；西部中线一些长而直的谷地为首次成图或向内陆延伸更远。格陵兰冰盖面积约 170 万平方公里、最厚处超过 3 公里，新图基于 ICESat-2 — ATLAS 等数据与 Chartrand et al. 的研究。"}}
{"id":"understand-geotech-esa-earth-explorer","capability":"understand","author":"GEOHOT 地理信息技术语料 agent（Wave 2，2026-09-29 按 industry/sources.json 登记的真实信源实抓核验）","what":"未入选（均值 51 > understandFloor 50）：仍按精选写法出稿。","match":{"urlIncludes":"Three_Earth_Explorer_candidates","titleIncludes":"Earth Explorer candidates"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.esa.int/Applications/Observing_the_Earth/FutureEO/Three_Earth_Explorer_candidates_go_forward","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"ESA Observing the Earth","title":"Three Earth Explorer candidates go forward","text":"Today, ESA’s Programme Board for Earth Observation took the decision to pave the way for three mission concepts to move forward to the next stage of development taking into account both their scientific relevance and programmatic considerations.\n\nThe decision follows the User Consultation Meeting held in July, where four mission concepts underwent detailed scrutiny by the scientific community. Building on the outcomes of this important consultation, ESA’s Advisory Committee for Earth Observation (ACEO) provided their advice on the scientific merits of each mission, ranking them in the following order: ECO, Keystone, CryoRad, Hydroterra+.\n\nRene Forsberg, on behalf of the ACEO, said, “ECO would target global mean Earth Energy Imbalance (EEI), the most fundamental climate variable, and widely recognised as the most important longstanding knowledge gap in quantifying ongoing climate change and would assess the effectiveness of climate mitigation measures.”\n\nAcknowledging the scientific and societal relevance of EEI, ESA and its Member States set science first by giving the extremely challenging ECO mission concept the opportunity to be further investigated in the framework of the Earth Explorer 12 activities.\n\nHighlighting the relevance of the Keystone concept, Prof. Forsberg noted, “By providing the first global direct observations of atomic oxygen together with co-located measurements of temperature, wind and relevant atmospheric constituents in the 50–250 km altitude range, Keystone would address fundamental knowledge gaps in this underexplored part of the atmosphere.”\n\nAs an additional benefit, Keystone would also detect metal from space debris entering the atmosphere, which is projected to increase exponentially in the future.\n\nFurthermore, ACEO recognised the compelling objectives of the CryoRad concept, which would directly measure temperatures and basal conditions within the polar ice sheets. These measurements would provide data for understanding ice-sheet dyna"},"reply":{"itemType":"technology_release","authorRole":"principal","tags":["技术与软件","遥感影像","欧空局"],"editorialJudgment":"未入选但高于 understandFloor：候选任务晋级是 Earth Explorer 12 时间线上的节点，ACEO 排序与任务目标（EEI、原子氧）都是实参，但今天还没有新的观测能力交付给使用者，act 只给 3。","titleZh":"欧洲空间局（ESA）选出 ECO、Keystone、CryoRad 三个地球探测者候选任务","summaryZh":"欧洲空间局（ESA）地球观测计划委员会决定让 ECO、Keystone、CryoRad 三个候选任务进入下一准备阶段，向第 12 颗地球探测者（Earth Explorer 12）推进。顾问委员会（ACEO）按科学价值排序为 ECO、Keystone、CryoRad、Hydroterra+，其中 ECO 面向全球平均地球能量不平衡（EEI）。"}}
